#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD2247 expect=noViolation domain=TS
#note "Row 1 is a complete ISO date, row 2 a partial (year-month) ISO date - and this row is the load-bearing contrast with the landed PMDA-SD2247A-invalid_partial_date-TS.cdt, where the SAME shape FIRES because that rule tests completeness, not validity. Row 3 carries a non-ISO value under a different parameter (DCUTDTC), which is outside this rule's condition."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset TS label="Trial Summary"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col TSSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col TSPARMCD type=Char label="Trial Summary Parameter Short Name"
col TSPARM   type=Char label="Trial Summary Parameter"
col TSVAL    type=Char label="Parameter Value"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | TS | 1 | SSTDTC  | Study Start Date | 2020-01-15
CDISCPILOT01 | TS | 2 | SSTDTC  | Study Start Date | 2021-03
CDISCPILOT01 | TS | 1 | DCUTDTC | Data Cutoff Date | 30JUN2020
